                    insight_built:          `Ecosystem built: you answered the disruptor with a separate, ecosystem-built engine — relevant to the growth segment, co-created with durable partners, and funded beyond the seed. This is the Christensen-correct response, executed.`,
                    insight_noyear2:        `Bright launch, no Year 2: relevance climbed but sustainability is thin. You showed a launch, not a business — the first cohort breaks even in month 14 and there is no credible bridge. This is the trajectory the board is afraid of.`,
                    insight_fragile:        `Relevant but fragile: the flagship lands in the right segment, yet weak partnerships or a thin capability base leave it dependent and exposed. Relevance without ecosystem strength does not survive the second year.`,
                    insight_short:          `You fell short of the relevance the board demanded. Most likely you polished the legacy core, refused to choose a segment, or mispriced against SkillForge — and the school stays structurally out-positioned in the fastest-growing segment.`,
                    insight_lowsustain:     `Sustainability is low — the plan reads as a project, not a durable business. Without a break-even bridge, a reinvestment logic, and a decision on what to stop, the flagship decays once the seed runs out.`,
                    insight_lowecosystem:   `Ecosystem strength is weak — you built mostly alone or surrendered control to a platform. Relevance in management education comes from value co-created across employers, alumni, public bodies and technology partners, not from a single node.`,
                    insight_lowenrol:       `Projected enrolment is thin. A credible flagship needs a segment that exists and will pay; revisit the where-to-play choice, the price point and the partnership that brings the pipeline.`,
                    insight_exemplary:      `Exemplary: relevance, ecosystem strength and sustainability moved together to a board-ready position. Two years out, the early indicators say the flagship is winning the disrupted segment — and funding its own future.`,
